.TH SNAPD 8
.SH NAME
snapd \- daily vac snapshots of /usr into the local venti store
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B snapd
[
.B -1
] [
.B -a
.I addr
] [
.B -p
.I tree
] [
.B -m
.I maxdatasize
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Snapd
archives the durable trees into the snapshot venti store as one vac
archive, once shortly after startup and then daily; with
.B -1
it takes a single snapshot and exits.
The default set is
.B /usr
plus the configuration overlays that live outside it:
.BR /lib/ndb ,
.BR /lib/lucifer/theme ,
.B /lib/veltro
and
.BR /lib/keyring ,
each captured as the namespace sees it (the durable overlay side
first). Repeatable
.B -p
options replace the set.
Note that keyring files are archived: scores from this store name key
material, exactly as the host-side
.B ~/.infernode/lib/keyring
files do; the store is localhost-only.
Each snapshot appends one line \(em a timestamp and a
.B vac:
score \(em to
.BR /usr/inferno/snapshots/log ;
the most recent outcome is written to
.BR /usr/inferno/snapshots/status .
A snapshot names an immutable tree: mount it read-only with
.IR vacfs (4)
or extract files with
.IR vacget (1).
Identical content dedupes in the store, so a snapshot costs only what
changed.
.PP
Durability of
.B /usr
does not depend on snapshots \(em it comes from the
.B ~/.infernode
overlay (see
.BR /doc/PERSISTENCE.md ).
Snapshots add history: the dump filesystem's role.
.PP
Before each snapshot the store's data file (found via the
.B ventistore
environment variable, set by the boot profile) is checked against
.IR maxdatasize ;
past 80% a warning is written to the status file and, when the install
audits, to the audit log.
The store is write-once \(em reclaiming space means starting a fresh
store.
.PP
The boot profile starts
.I snapd
and its
.IR ventisrv (8)
when
.B /usr/inferno/snapshots/on
exists (Settings \(-> Snapshots).
The store lives outside
.B /usr
\(em a snapshot must not contain its own store \(em on the canonical
venti port
.BR tcp!127.0.0.1!17034 .
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/snapd.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR ventisrv (8),
.IR vacfs (4),
.IR vacget (1),
.IR auditprov (2)
